{"file":{"content":"Strip away the manuscripts' layers and the obstruction is one thing. Collatz (mod cycles) is equivalent to bounded \ndeficit: along every odd orbit, the cumulative 2-adic valuation tracks the irrational slope with bounded error,\n$$D_m ;=; m\\log_2 3 ;+; O(1)\\qquad\\text{i.e.}\\qquad E_m=D_m-m\\log_2 3 \\text{ stays bounded.}$$\nHere $D_m=\\sum_{i<m}v_2(3x_i{+}1)$ is determined entirely by the integer's 2-adic structure, and $\\log_2 3$ is the\nequilibrium slope. So the obstruction is:\n\n▎ Every integer's deterministic valuation sequence equidistributes against the $\\log_2 3$ rotation strongly enough to \n▎ shadow the equilibrium line with bounded fluctuation — never sustaining the rare large-deviation excursions (high \n▎ ascents = $C_6$; sub-equilibrium tails = stabilized residue clusters) that a summable-rate Borel–Cantelli count says \n▎ are negligible.\n\nEverything we measured is one face of this: the height cocycle $M(s)=3^s/(2^{1+s}-1)$, the Cramér root $s^*{=}1$, the\n$2^{-H}$ tail, the post-exit taboo — all are the annealed law of this cocycle. The gap is always the same: annealed \n(Haar-measure / a.e.) is easy and true; quenched (this one integer orbit) is the wall.\n\nThe name\n\nIt is a deterministic (quenched) equidistribution / large-deviation–Borel–Cantelli statement for a non-invertible,\nnon-uniformly-hyperbolic arithmetic cocycle — equivalently, a single-orbit normality statement: that the\nparity/valuation sequence of every integer is \"normal\" (pseudorandom enough) with respect to the $\\times 2$,$\\times 3$\ndynamics. The program's own Lean development already names it correctly — the open sorry is\nequidistribution_implies_deficit_bounded / cellSeqNu2_equidistributed. That is the obstruction, formalized.\n\n\nWhy it is genuinely irreducible (not just hard-for-us)\n\nIt sits in a gap where the three theories that could close it each fail a hypothesis — and the failures are structural,\nwhich is what the dead-end graveyard kept rediscovering:\n\n1. Dynamical Borel–Cantelli (Chernov–Kleinbock, Dolgopyat–Fayad–Liu): needs mixing / decay of correlations w.r.t. an\ninvariant measure — and delivers an a.e. conclusion. We have no proven mixing for the deterministic map, and we need\nevery orbit, not a.e. (That's exactly why the generic-sampling route and the post-exit pressure route both died on\nmeasurement.)\n2. Measure rigidity (Furstenberg $\\times2,\\times3$, Rudolph–Johnson, Lindenstrauss, EKL): needs two independent \npositive-entropy commuting actions. The program found the decisive structural fact (pvt_14/15): the cocycle is\n$\\times2$-rich but rank-one / rigid in the $\\times3$ direction — one factor of 3 per step, no independent\n$\\times3$-entropy. So the rigidity machinery has nothing to grip, and again it produces measure statements, not\nevery-orbit ones.\n3. Homogeneous nondivergence / effective equidistribution (Kleinbock–Margulis, EMV, BLMV): needs an $S$-arithmetic \nhomogeneous-space encoding of the orbit and target. No such encoding exists for the Collatz cocycle; that's an analogy,\nnot a tool.\n\nSo it is not that we haven't found the right lemma. The obstruction has the form of all three theories and the\nhypotheses of none.\n\n\nThe deepest honest framing\n\nAt bottom this is an instance of the deterministic-versus-random barrier — the \"a specific deterministic sequence realizesthe\nstatistics its generating dynamics predicts\" phenomenon. It is the same type of statement as: the digits of $\\pi$ are\nequidistributed; $\\sqrt 2$ is normal; a specific algebraic number's base-$b$ expansion is pseudorandom. These are believed\ntrue, follow trivially in the annealed/measure sense, and have no general method in the quenched/pointwise sense. Tao's 2022\nresult is the frontier marker: it does the average (\"almost all orbits\") via the $\\mathbb Z/3^n$ Fourier estimate, and\nexplicitly cannot reach the pointwise statement. The pointwise statement is our wall.\n\nSo, to name it crisply:\n\n▎ The Collatz obstruction is the quenched equidistribution (deterministic normality) of the accelerated map's valuation\n▎ cocycle against the $\\log_2 3$ rotation — a single-orbit large-deviation–Borel–Cantelli theorem for a $\\times2$-entropy,\n▎ $\\times3$-rank-one arithmetic system — which is one sharply-pinned instance of the general deterministic-pseudorandomness\n▎ barrier, for which no current theory suffices.\n\nnone.\n\nThe deepest honest framing\n\nAt bottom this is an instance of the deterministic-versus-random barrier — the \"a specific deterministic sequence realizes\nthe statistics its generating dynamics predicts\" phenomenon. It is the same type of statement as: the digits of $\\pi$ are\nequidistributed; $\\sqrt 2$ is normal; a specific algebraic number's base-$b$ expansion is pseudorandom. These are believed\ntrue, follow trivially in the annealed/measure sense, and have no general method in the quenched/pointwise sense. Tao's 2022\nresult is the frontier marker: it does the average (\"almost all orbits\") via the $\\mathbb Z/3^n$ Fourier estimate, and\nexplicitly cannot reach the pointwise statement. The pointwise statement is our wall.\n\nSo, to name it crisply:\n\n▎ The Collatz obstruction is the quenched equidistribution (deterministic normality) of the accelerated map's valuation\n▎ cocycle against the $\\log_2 3$ rotation — a single-orbit large-deviation–Borel–Cantelli theorem for a $\\times2$-entropy,\n▎ $\\times3$-rank-one arithmetic system — which is one sharply-pinned instance of the general deterministic-pseudorandomness\n▎ barrier, for which no current theory suffices.\nnone.\n\nThe deepest honest framing\n\nSo it is not that we haven't found the right lemma. The obstruction has the form of all three theories and the hypotheses\nof none.\n\nThe honest hedge\n\nThis is the program's reduction, not a theorem that Collatz equals exactly this. It is conditional on the reduction arrows\n(which are proved-modulo-named-inputs, not all watertight) and on cycle elimination being separable. What the program can\nclaim with confidence is the negative half, which the dead-ends establish: the obstruction is not finite-state, not\nlocal-arithmetic, not finite-character, not a rank function, not a spectral gap, not a mixing/Borel–Cantelli estimate, and\nnot a fractal-geometry target. By elimination and by the five-fold convergence, what remains is exactly the\nquenched-equidistribution / deterministic-normality statement above.\n\n","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/collatz/docs/why_collatz_fails.md","numLines":96,"startLine":1,"totalLines":96},"type":"text"}